Z||000001||WKDFIRO||11-25-2000||05:59 AM||||I had read in some articles where the Opel Speedster would get a corporate cousin in Vauxhall. Even then they would sell a total of around 4000 vehicles a year. Among all the other reasons given why it might not come to U.S. is those numbers are ridiculously low given the insane expectation of selling 100,000 Fieros a year that GM expected out of Pontiac.<P>Can you imagine half a million Fieros on the street in the 5 years of production? You would see a Fiero at every streetlight at that rate!<P>Me, I get sick of seeing that many Hondas, I like only seeing the occasional Fiero.||||reg||4
